c language, with over 80% of the local population speaking Welsh. Caernarfon provides a good base for visiting other places of interest in North Wales.","grounding":[{"source":"wikivoyage","title":"Caernarfon","url":"https://en.wikivoyage.org/wiki/Caernarfon","licence":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}],"short":"Caernarfon is a Royal town in Gwynedd, North-West Wales. Caernarfon Castle, Snowdon and Menai Suspension Bridge lead its 12 sights. A full day covers it, ideally in June to August. The historic centre is on the World Heritage list.","short_src":"composed","facts":{"population":9730,"visit_h":6}},"highlights":[{"id":"hl-caernarfon-castle","name":"Caernarfon Castle","kind":"Castle","lat":53.13931,"lon":-4.27689,"dist_km":0.5,"rank_score":11.56,"resolved_by":"catalogue","fact":"Medieval fortress in Gwynedd, Wales","image":{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4a/Castell_Caernarfon_yn_y_cyfnos_yn_2023_-_Castell_Caernarfon%2C_Gwynedd%2C_Wales_at_Dusk_-_2023_10.png/960px-Castell_Caernarfon_yn_y_cyfnos_yn_2023_-_Castell_Caernarfon%2C_Gwynedd%2C_Wales_at_Dusk_-_2023_10.png","author":"Llywelyn2000","licence":"CC BY-SA 4.0","licence_url":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Castell_Caernarfon_yn_y_cyfnos_yn_2023_-_Castell_Caernarfon,_Gwynedd,_Wales_at_Dusk_-_2023_10.png","w":3840,"h":2160,"ok_print":true},"wikipedia":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Caernarfon_Castle"},{"id":"hl-snowdon","name":"Snowdon","kind":"Peak","lat":53.06886,"lon":-4.07559,"dist_km":15.3,"rank_score":10.46,"resolved_by":"catalogue","image":{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c0/Snowdon_from_Llyn_Llydaw.jpg/960px-Snowdon_from_Llyn_Llydaw.jpg","author":"User:Gdr","licence":"CC BY-SA 3.0","licence_url":"http://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/3.0/","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Snowdon_from_Llyn_Llydaw.jpg","w":1536,"h":2048,"ok_print":true}},{"id":"hl-menai-suspension-bridge","name":"M