ing Constantinople to make a point about who was in charge. World Heritage listed with his other Welsh castles, and it holds the Royal Welch Fusiliers museum as well.","evidence":{"n_sources":9,"of":12,"urls":["https://www.dafyddhardy.co.uk/articles/attractions-in-caernarfon","https://www.gonorthwales.co.uk/things-to-do/caernarfon-castle-p366311","https://www.caernarfon.com/exploring-caernarfon-the-best-things-to-do-in-this-charming-welsh-town/"],"method":"web"},"sources":["web"]},{"name":"Welsh Highland Railway","type":"activity","detail":"The longest heritage railway in Britain: 25 miles from under the castle walls, climbing over 650 ft on the flank of Snowdon, then zigzagging down to Beddgelert and through the Aberglaslyn pass to Porthmadog.","link":"https://www.visitwales.com/attraction/train/welsh-highland-railway-571421","evidence":{"n_sources":7,"of":12,"urls":["https://www.visitmidwales.co.uk/things-to-do/welsh-highland-railway-p1716301","https://www.visitwales.com/attraction/train/welsh-highland-railway-571421","https://www.gonorthwales.co.uk/things-to-do/welsh-highland-railway-p366171"],"method":"web"},"sources":["web"]},{"name":"Walk the town walls","type":"activity","detail":"The 13th century wall still rings the old town, and the circuit gives you the castle, the harbour and the water in one go.","evidence":{"n_sources":6,"of":12,"urls":["https://www.dafyddhardy.co.uk/articles/attractions-in-caernarfon","https://www.visitwales.com/destinations/north-wales/things-do-caernarfon","https://www.emilyluxton.co.uk/best-things-to-do-in-caernarfon-wales/"],"method":"web"},"sources":["web"]},{"name":"Segontium Roman fort","type":"activity","detail":"The Romans held this crossing for three centuries before the castle existed; the fort's footings are up the hill behind the town.","evidence":{"n_sources":4,"of":12,"urls":["https://www.visitwales.com/destinations/north-wales/things-do-caernarfon","https://www.emilyluxton.co.uk/best-things-to-do-in-caernarfon-wales/",